  "notes": "The kapok passenger scheme (CSN/standard) with cargo titles in place of the airline's: '中国南方货运航空' high forward and 'CHINA SOUTHERN CARGO' lower, ahead of the wing (on the airliners 'CHINA SOUTHERN' sits beside the Chinese over the windows). Measured on B-222W (left, 2025-05-26). The cheatline is the airliners'; a small 'BOEING 777F' sits on it aft, not drawn. No winglets on the 777F. Measured on the A350 (B-32ED, left) and A321neo (B-32L7, right); the 737 MAX and 787 carry the same layout. The wing undersides carry '中国南方航空' (and 'CHINA SOUTHERN' on the other wing, not drawn here). A small 'AIRBUS A350-900' / 'BOEING 737-8' type name sits on the navy band aft, not drawn. Colors by eye. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the English title runs about 0.18 (B-222W; a perspective photo, so the share is a little uncertain), its capitals about 0.15 tall (they were drawn 0.21, which set them condensed at that length).",
  "history": "New file. China Southern's freighters (777F since 2009) wear the passenger scheme with cargo titles."
